  "id": "COMPOUND:38029 - PROTEIN:79",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol and Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha, mediated through multiple pathways. The compound 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol is identified as a target of RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase, which in turn is targeted by trans-Norbixin. This pathway leads to the interaction of 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol with Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha. Additionally, 2-Phenylpropan-1-Ol is also shown to target Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2, which is targeted by Wikstromol, further linking this compound to the Interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, with scores indicating a moderate level of confidence in the relationship. The mechanisms involve kinase targeting and receptor interaction, suggesting a possible role in signaling pathways related to interleukin-11 receptor function. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential involvement in regulatory processes involving the interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha.",
